pytest-httpx2 is a pytest plugin that mocks out httpx2 using respx.

It registers an "httpcore2" respx mocker, which patches the httpcore2
connection and proxy classes that httpx2 dispatches through, and exposes an
httpx2_mock fixture returning a respx router. Tests configure the router with
the standard respx API, so an existing respx suite can cover httpx2 clients
without a separate mocking layer.
